# Digital Evidence Management & Chain of Custody System

A web-based platform for cyber forensic investigators to securely manage digital evidence, maintain chain of custody, collaborate on findings, and generate court-ready forensic reports.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **MongoDB**: The plan assumes you have MongoDB installed locally or have a MongoDB Atlas connection string ready. Please confirm which you prefer.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **AI Summarization**: The synopsis mentions Python + Transformers for AI summarization. For this initial build, I'll implement a **mock AI summarization endpoint** within the Node.js backend (using simple extractive summarization) to avoid the complexity of a separate Python microservice. We can add a real Python/Transformers service as a future enhancement. **Do you want the real Python service now, or is the mock approach acceptable?**

> [!WARNING]
> **File Storage**: Evidence files (disk images, logs, etc.) will be stored on the **local filesystem** under `d:\CAPSTRONE\server\uploads\`. For production, you'd want cloud storage (S3, Azure Blob). Is local storage acceptable for now?

---

